5. Terminology Rules

The following rules apply throughout the Atlas ecosystem.

Every defined term SHALL have exactly one canonical definition.
Specifications SHALL reference canonical definitions rather than redefining them.
New concepts SHALL be introduced through Atlas Core Concepts before being referenced by other specifications.
Terminology SHALL remain technology independent.
Synonyms SHOULD be avoided unless explicitly defined.
6. Conformance

A specification conforms to the Atlas Glossary if it:

Uses canonical terminology consistently.
References Atlas Core Concepts where appropriate.
Avoids conflicting definitions.
Preserves semantic consistency across the framework.
7. Future Evolution

Additional glossary entries MAY be introduced as new canonical concepts are added to the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework.

Existing canonical definitions SHALL NOT be modified incompatibly without a formal versioned revision.